From b53ab44ec901cb5d882a9cd218fc18816e90a83f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 13:29:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [Channel Selection]Changes to enable Channel Selection with
 active ACS

Active ACS Channel Selection: Introduces a new agent config
flag "active_acs_chansel_enable" that, when set together with the existing
"enable_auto_chansel_handling", makes the Airties/third-party controller
handling path actually drive the QCA driver ACS on nl80211 (QMESH OpenWrt)
instead of the previous no-op stub.

Behaviour:
- enable_auto_chansel_handling=1, active_acs_chansel_enable=0
    -> unchanged. build_acs_list() collects the controller's non-operable
       (preference==0) exclude channels and start_platform_acs() on nl80211
       remains the historical stub (returns false).
- enable_auto_chansel_handling=1, active_acs_chansel_enable=1
    -> On CHANNEL_SELECTION_REQUEST with a preferred channel list:
       build_acs_list() computes the block list as "all channels of the
       radio (radio->channels_list) minus the preferred set" (preferred =
       controller preference != 0; empty operable op-class lists expand to
       all channels of the op-class), keyed per 20MHz operating class.
       nl80211 start_platform_acs() then drives the driver ACS on the base
       radio interface over wpa_ctrl:
         acs clear_block_chan_list
         acs set_block_chan_list <non-preferred channels>
         acs invoke 0            (DynamicACS + CSA)
       The driver selects a channel from the remaining (preferred, non-
       blocked) set and performs the CSA. The existing AP-CSA-FINISHED ->
       CSA_Finished -> CSA notification -> Operating Channel Report flow is
       reused unchanged.
- enable_auto_chansel_handling=0
    -> active_acs_chansel_enable is ignored (FLAG=0 internal scoring stays).

The flag is propagated to the bwl HAL via hal_conf_t (bwl does not include
AgentDB), set in ap_manager::create_ap_wlan_hal().

Exhaustive [ACTIVE_ACS]-tagged debug logs are added across the flow: config
values at startup and at HAL creation, the full parsed controller preference
map, the computed preferred set (+count), the full radio channel list
(+count), the computed block list (per op-class, flattened, total), and every
acs clear/set/invoke command issued to the driver (with success/failure and a
block-list read-back).

Signed-off-by: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
